-id "q-279444" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${B}^{2}.$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\">${B}^{2}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-5}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "To find ${B}^{2},$ we multiply $B$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186604585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29db0dc6-d441-5d4b-bdd6-7056a72eab43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604253} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2f1d3d-5ae8-58a5-8527-f854e40bc5b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 18 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604313} {:answer/id #uuid "a4cd98ba-a4a0-5733-b236-6b9819eafcc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 18 \\\\ 27 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604389} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fb4363-d906-5d63-b8f5-ca5ece22e23d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 18 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604416} {:answer/id #uuid "f64eef86-9144-52f3-88b0-259695e36555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & -2 \\\\ 27 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4cd98ba-a4a0-5733-b236-6b9819eafcc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 18 \\\\ 27 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604389} :answer-field/id #uuid "b13dac53-37a8-5fdf-a5b9-20114b11adce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186604533}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47f77f53-d24f-5514-bb7f-871f8600f6ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-78339" :question/problem "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${C}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${C}^{2},$ we multiply $C$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${C}^{3}={C}^{2}\\cdot C,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{3} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & 18 \\\\ 27 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b41f8447-f404-563a-8e9c-ea5233e6684f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629008}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b41f8447-f404-563a-8e9c-ea5233e6684f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218662