\end{bmatrix}.$ Find ${G}^{4}.$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${G}^{4}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${G}^{2},$ we multiply $G$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{G}^{2} & =G\\cdot G \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${G}^{4}={G}^{2}\\cdot {G}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{G}^{4} & ={G}^{2}\\cdot {G}^{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 \\\\ -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0856b871-0665-5614-bffc-692aa7a91cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 10 \\\\ -15 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628720} {:answer/id #uuid "627ee62a-5db2-5077-b133-e78d07d3bea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 11 \\\\ -15 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628875} {:answer/id #uuid "875825ab-c974-5c20-981b-2b7e3fe64542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 16 \\\\ -15 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628937} {:answer/id #uuid "c606bf37-3c0d-5a95-8ba4-1968867cbbc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 10 \\\\ -16 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629041} {:answer/id #uuid "f5765fb7-81b8-515f-beba-48c107fee636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 10 \\\\ 11 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0856b871-0665-5614-bffc-692aa7a91cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 10 \\\\ -15 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628720} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7298e0-647c-5293-be5a-8257e72f0cff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629191}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "82f52676-5e6a-5fb8-b917-230ddfc7b240" :question/math-academy-id "q-78498" :question/problem "If $T=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${T}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${T}^{2},$ we multiply $T$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{2} & =T\\cdot T \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${T}^{3}={T}^{2}\\cdot T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{3} & ={T}^{2}\\cdot T \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 10 \\\\ -15 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca1ccbbe-4763-5abc-90a8-57b33948706a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca1ccbbe-4763-5abc-90a8-57b33948706a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629048} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4aa99d-d180-57b7-9800-2a9dbef25cef" :answer-field/key "fiel